        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Intro",
            "id": 76783,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can use comparisons to check if a string is equal to or not equal to another string.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;online&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" == \" /><text value=\"&quot;online&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;online&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" != \" /><text value=\"&quot;offline&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"True\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"True\" /></content></output></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Equality operator",
            "id": 76781,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To check if a string is equal to another string, we also use the <strong>equality operator</strong>, <code>==</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;apple&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" == \" /><text value=\"&quot;apple&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"14\" endIndex=\"16\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&lt;=\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"True\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>==</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To check if a string is equal to another string, we use the <strong>equality operator</strong>.</p><p>Compare the two strings so the code prints <code>True</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;apple&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" == \" /><text value=\"&quot;apple&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"14\" endIndex=\"16\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"=\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"!=\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"True\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>==</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "True",
            "id": 76772,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>If the string on the left is equal to the string on the right, as in <code>\"apple\" == \"apple\"</code>, the result is <code>True</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;apple&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" == \" /><text value=\"&quot;apple&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"13\" /><option startIndex=\"14\" endIndex=\"16\" /><option startIndex=\"17\" endIndex=\"24\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"True\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>\"apple\"</code>, followed by <code>==</code>, and finally <code>\"apple\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Two strings are equal when they contain exactly the same text.</p><p>Fill the gaps so the comparison prints <code>True</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;apple&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" == \" /><text value=\"&quot;apple&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"13\" /><option startIndex=\"14\" endIndex=\"16\" /><option startIndex=\"17\" endIndex=\"24\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;orange&quot;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;apples&quot;\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"True\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>\"apple\"</code>, followed by <code>==</code>, and finally <code>\"apple\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "False",
            "id": 76771,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>If the string on the left isn't equal to the string on the right, as in <code>\"apple\" == \"orange\"</code>, the result is <code>False</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;apple&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" == \" /><text value=\"&quot;orange&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"14\" endIndex=\"16\" /><option startIndex=\"17\" endIndex=\"25\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"False\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>==</code>, followed by <code>\"orange\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When two strings are different, checking them for equality gives <code>False</code>.</p><p>Compare <code>\"apple\"</code> against a different fruit so the code prints <code>False</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;apple&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" == \" /><text value=\"&quot;orange&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"14\" endIndex=\"16\" /><option startIndex=\"17\" endIndex=\"25\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"!=\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;apple&quot;\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"False\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>==</code>, followed by <code>\"orange\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Comparing the same string",
            "id": 76782,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can also compare variables that store strings with each other, like in <code>fruit_1 == fruit_2</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"fruit_1 = \" /><text value=\"&quot;apple&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"fruit_2 = \" /><text value=\"&quot;orange&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(fruit_1 == fruit_2)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"45\" endIndex=\"52\" /><option startIndex=\"53\" endIndex=\"55\" /><option startIndex=\"56\" endIndex=\"63\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"False\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>fruit_1</code>, followed by <code>==</code>, and finally <code>fruit_2</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can also compare two variables that store strings, like in <code>fruit_1 == fruit_2</code>.</p><p>Compare the fruit variables, with <code>fruit_1</code> on the left, so the code prints <code>False</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"fruit_1 = \" /><text value=\"&quot;apple&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"fruit_2 = \" /><text value=\"&quot;orange&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(fruit_1 == fruit_2)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"45\" endIndex=\"52\" /><option startIndex=\"53\" endIndex=\"55\" /><option startIndex=\"56\" endIndex=\"63\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"=\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"fruit_3\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"False\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>fruit_1</code>, followed by <code>==</code>, and finally <code>fruit_2</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 1",
            "id": 76780,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What does the equality operator, <code>==</code>, do?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">It checks if a string is equal to another string</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">It checks if a string is greater than another string</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">It checks if a string is equal to another string.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A program checks <code>\"sun\" == \"sunset\"</code>. What is the comparison asking?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Whether both strings are exactly the same</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Whether the first string comes before the second one</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Whether the second string begins with the first one</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Whether both strings are exactly the same.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 2",
            "id": 76779,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Which of these is the equality operator?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>==</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>=</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>==</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>You want to check whether <code>color</code> stores <code>\"red\"</code>. Which operator belongs in the comparison?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>==</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>=</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>!=</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>==</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 3",
            "id": 76778,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What does this display in the console?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;LED+&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" == \" /><text value=\"&quot;LED&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"False\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>False</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>True</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>False</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The output shown is for <code>\"LED+\" == \"LED\"</code>.</p><p>If you change the right string to <code>\"LED+\"</code>, what will the code display?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;LED+&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" == \" /><text value=\"&quot;LED&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"False\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>True</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>False</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>\"LED+\"</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>True</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 4",
            "id": 76777,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Which of these comparisons results in <code>True</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>\"apple\" == \"apple\"</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>\"apple\" == \"orange\"</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\"><code>\"apple\" == \"apple\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A comparison with <code>==</code> should result in <code>True</code>. Which one does that?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>\"apple\" == \"apple\"</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>\"apple\" == \"orange\"</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>\"apple\" = \"apple\"</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>\"apple\" == \"apple\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
